<main id="main-content"><section class="page-hero"><div class="wrap"><p class="eyebrow">ABOUT OUR CLUB</p><h1>Avon Toastmasters<br><em>in Christchurch.</em></h1><p class="lead">Avon Toastmasters is a Christchurch club where people come together to practise communication, build confidence and support each other's progress.</p></div></section><section class="heritage heritage-about"><div class="wrap heritage-inner"><div><p class="eyebrow">PROUDLY PART OF CHRISTCHURCH</p><h2>More than 50 years of helping people find their voice.</h2><p>Avon Toastmasters was chartered on 1 September 1974 and has been part of the Christchurch community for more than five decades. Through changing times and generations, the heart of the club remains the same: people learning together, encouraging one another and becoming more confident communicators and leaders.</p><p>Our charter date is a milestone in a story shaped by the members who have contributed their time, ideas, speeches, encouragement and leadership over the years — and by the people who will join us next.</p></div></div></section><section class="section"><div class="wrap two-col"><div><p class="eyebrow blue">WHO WE ARE</p><h2>Different people.<br><em>Shared ambition.</em></h2></div><div class="copy"><p class="large">You might be preparing for presentations at work, finding your feet in a new role, studying, running a business or simply wanting to feel more comfortable speaking in a group.</p><p>Toastmasters offers a practical way to improve: you learn by taking part. Members support one another through prepared speeches, impromptu speaking, meeting roles and thoughtful evaluations. You can start small and build at a pace that suits you.</p><p>Avon is a local club in the worldwide Toastmasters network. Our meetings are organised by members and shaped by the people who take part.</p></div></div></section><section class="section tint"><div class="wrap"><div class="section-head"><div><p class="eyebrow blue">OUR APPROACH</p><h2>Learn by doing.<br><em>Grow together.</em></h2></div><p>We believe the best way to become more confident is to practise in a place where it is safe to try, make mistakes, receive feedback and try again.</p></div><div class="tiles"><article><span>01</span><h3>Welcoming</h3><p>Guests are welcome to observe and get to know the club before making a decision.</p></article><article><span>02</span><h3>Practical</h3><p>Meetings give you real opportunities to speak, listen, organise and lead.</p></article><article><span>03</span><h3>Encouraging</h3><p>Feedback focuses on what is working and what you can try next.</p></article><article><span>04</span><h3>Member-led</h3><p>Members contribute to meetings and help one another make progress.</p></article></div></div></section><section class="section"><div class="wrap callout"><div><p class="eyebrow blue">FIND YOUR PEOPLE</p><h2>Come and experience<br><em>Avon for yourself.</em></h2></div><a class="btn btn-blue" href="/visit.html">Plan a guest visit →</a></div></section></main>